## Fixes in the commit

- F671 (lesson-flow.tsx, week-view.tsx): the pure helper splitThaiRuns (next to pickLang and
  noteLangsOf) splits a string into runs of Thai script (U+0E00 to U+0E7F) and other text;
  the renderer LanguageRuns wraps each Thai run of an English text in a span with lang="th"
  and renders a Thai text as one plain run under its own lang="th" element. The flow uses it
  on every English render of week data (note lines, variant lines, loop panel fields, sight
  words, share labels and captions, recall ask and cards, opening prompts, step and day
  titles, media titles); the week view imports it for the title, the sound, the phonemic
  awareness skill, the frame, the tricky words, the family words and captions, and the lesson
  titles. content/ is untouched; the committed F671 red case passes without an edit.
- F641 and F661 (docs/runbooks/storytime-deploy.md, flag section only): the flag flow of a
  new build is one numbered list inside the flag-state bullet (1. sign in on the tag URL
  host, 2. open the tag URL of the new build, 3. compare the names, 4. on 200 run the off
  command with the new build image, 5. check 404 and the names on the off revision, 6. name
  that revision in step 4). The sentence "The values are compared only for the flag" is
  replaced by: the names compare shows that no env name differs except
  STORYTIME_TEACHER_ROUTES, and the flag state shows only through the 200 or 404 check of
  /th/teacher/2/1 on the tag URL. The text states that each names-only command prints one
  line with the names separated by ";", and keeps "prints the variable names, not their
  values". Every command, --no-traffic, the tags, Daniel's go, and the way back stay. No
  gcloud command ran; the runbook is text only.

